 # Setup decisions

The accepted outcome of the setup map ([#1](https://github.com/Kucze3205/ConnectWithLabview/issues/1)). It replaces `setup-notes.md`, which the arming ticket ([#8](https://github.com/Kucze3205/ConnectWithLabview/issues/8)) deleted. Owner decisions are kept here together with the specific guarantees they lose and what replaces each one. A lost guarantee informs the owner's choice; it is not a veto. Evidence and details stay in the linked files. After arming, only the owner changes these decisions (`docs/perpetua/engine.md`, "Authority after arming").

## Owner decisions

| Date | Decision | Where it lives |
|---|---|---|
| 18 Oct 2026 | Cloud-only execution. The owner's computer is never a runner. GitHub Actions and GitHub issue owner requests stay; Claude, Codex and Copilot accounts are all supported. MCP is not a fixed delivery form. | [environment.md](environment.md), `engine.yml` |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Private, non-commercial project on LabVIEW 2026 Q1 Community Edition (licensed until 27 June 2027). Do not ask again. | [environment.md](environment.md) |
| 18 Oct 2026 | This repository stays public and holds all automation. A private control repository was rejected. No paid API, purchased quota, paid runner or storage. | [cloud-authentication.md](cloud-authentication.md), [accepted-limits.md](accepted-limits.md) |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Full goal scope: all LabVIEW code, projects and artifacts, all versions. LabVIEW 2024 is the accepted fallback only if all versions need substantially more time; the effort estimate and compatibility limits must be shown to the owner before that choice. No numeric threshold. | [goal/goal.md](../../goal/goal.md) |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Success principles (topic D): separate reading fidelity and grounded answers, independent expected answers, withheld cases, matched baselines, visible coverage and gaps. Numeric thresholds and an executable goal gate wait for a credible benchmark and a separate acceptance. | [goal/goal.md](../../goal/goal.md), [evaluation.md](evaluation.md) |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Starting evaluation (topic C): keep the owner change gate (`gate.kind: owner`). `policy/evaluator/` only checks evidence integrity and reports quality as unmeasured. | [evaluation.md](evaluation.md), `engine.yml`, `policy/evaluator/` |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Starting roles (topic E): researcher, benchmark, implementation and report-only reviewer, plus the orchestrator role, registered but not the shaper (1 Nov 2026 row); audit, evaluator, verifier and Policymaker in `policy/`. | [roles.md](roles.md), `execution/`, `policy/` |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Accepted limits (topic F): technical autonomy within existing tools and offline roles; private material, provider disclosure, new publication categories and extra spending need specific grants. | [accepted-limits.md](accepted-limits.md), `engine.yml` (`limits`) |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Starting parameters (topic G): 24 h without a closed iteration (owner waits excluded) means rollback and retry; 10 iterations without an accepted improvement means a notice and independent work continues. | [operating-parameters.md](operating-parameters.md), `engine.yml` (`params`), `policy/params.yml` |
| 18 Oct 2026 | Multi-provider integration accepted with the positive Claude task deferred ("załóż że działa albo odblokuj następne issue"). | [cloud-authentication.md](cloud-authentication.md) |
| 20 Oct 2026 | Design criterion: best quality per subscription quota consumed; wall-clock time only breaks ties. The Policymaker chooses models; nothing is hard-wired. | [model-selection.md](model-selection.md), `policy/params.yml` |
| 21 Oct 2026 | **Arming with #24 (M4b) still open.** The owner chose to skip the three live model-boundary tests and start the loop. See "Lost guarantees", row 3. | [validation.md](validation.md) |
| 1 Nov 2026 | **Engine 0.6.0 adopted in full, including the routed providers** (`/perpetua:update` 0.5.0 → 0.6.0): no session sandbox, the machine is the boundary (ADR-0006); every session, routed ones included, runs in the tokenless `session` job. See rows 1, 3, 7, 8 and 10. | [engine.md](engine.md) "Routed cloud execution", `session.yml` |
| 1 Nov 2026 | **No starting shaper (`shaper: null`).** The Policymaker decides how the execution layer is organized (shaper kind, parallel candidates, state machine, roles) and changes it when progress is insufficient, including `startup` reads and working memory of execution roles. Reason: the orchestrator failed 0003–0005 at its turn cap with no graph (reset notes 4, 7). Caveat: without a shaper an iteration needs Policymaker orders or fails; the engine limit is tracked in [Perpetua #309](https://github.com/Kucze3205/Perpetua/issues/309). | `policy/params.yml`, [reset-2026-10-28.md](reset-2026-10-28.md) |

